        "title": "Rear-Axle Pinion-Seal Leak Can Damage the Differential (Recall 07V589)",
        "description": "Certain 2005-2007 Cadillac CTS-V vehicles have a drive-axle differential seal that may leak because it did not meet GM specifications. Continued lubricant loss can increase differential noise, overheat bearings and, in an advanced case, allow the differential to jam or lock the drive wheels.",
        "solution": "Check the VIN and recall-completion history. GM campaign 07204C directs dealers to replace the affected drive-axle differential pinion seal; confirm current campaign status before service.",
        "severity": "high",
        "confidence": "high",
