        "title": "Service Suspension Message Can Come from a MagneRide Shock Connector (PI0430C)",
        "description": "GM PI0430C covers 2009-2014 Cadillac CTS-V vehicles with Magnetic Ride Control when the Service Suspension System message appears with DTC C0575, C0580, C0585 or C0590. A 90-degree electrical connector at the top of a shock actuator may be incompletely seated or partially disconnected; the bulletin does not establish universal shock failure.",
        "solution": "Follow PI0430C connector inspection, seating and circuit checks before replacing a shock absorber. Continue normal service-information diagnosis if the connector path does not resolve the message or DTC.",
